OL,3,ALibya's top religious authority rules
OL,4,Aagainst wearing Nike clothes
OL,5,
OL,6,FLibya's highest religious authority,
OL,7,Fthe Dar al-Ifta, has issued a ruling
OL,8,Fbanning Muslims from buying, selling or
OL,9,Fwearing clothing bearing the Nike logo.
OL,11,FThe ruling, issued by the Tripoli-based
OL,12,Finstitution, states that the US
OL,13,Fsportswear giant was named after the
OL,14,FGreek goddess of victory and that its
OL,15,Ffamous swoosh logo was inspired by her
OL,16,Fwings.
OL,18,FIt argued that wearing clothing
OL,19,Fdisplaying the logo amounted to
OL,20,Fpromoting symbols associated "with
OL,21,Fpolytheism," or the worship of more
OL,22,Fthan one god.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG14/40
